.env

# Any other local env file is a secret too. `.env.example` is a tracked
# template (docs tell people to `cp .env.example .env`), so it is re-included.
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local QA workspace: rendered QA fixtures, extracted frames, contact sheets and
# QA reports. These are build/QA artifacts (several MB of PNGs/MP4s) kept on disk
# for review but intentionally untracked. Regenerate with:
#     python3 -m agent_system render-qa
#
# NOTE: output/ is deliberately NOT ignored — committed job artifacts under
# output/jobs/<id>/ (delivery_report.md, evidence_ledger.csv, preview.mp4, ...)
# are real deliverables in this project.
qa/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime service state — machine-local, not source and not a deliverable.
#
# These files are written continuously by the running bot/service. They change
# on every interaction, are not reproducible from the repository, and the job
# database and log have contained a real personal Telegram user id. They stay
# on disk (the service needs them) but are intentionally untracked.
#
# The SQLite sidecars (-shm shared-memory index, -wal write-ahead log) are part
# of the same database and must be excluded together with it: committing a
# database without its WAL can look like data loss.
#
# output/jobs/<id>/ is still tracked; this only excludes the database and logs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
output/jobs.sqlite3
output/jobs.sqlite3-shm
output/jobs.sqlite3-wal
output/logs/bot.log
output/logs/*.log
